        "problem": "What is the $y$-intercept of $y = -2e^{-2x}+3 ?$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x = 0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2{e}^{-2(0)}+3 \\\\  & =-2{e}^{0}+3 \\\\  & =-2(1)+3 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $1.$",
